Subject: [PATCH] Default to Escape prefix mode

Keep Escape as a prefix until the next key arrives, avoiding the
single-Escape timeout when using Esc-Esc and Esc-Enter on the target.
Users can still enable single-Escape mode in their personal configuration.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distribution default]

--- a/lib/tty/key.c
+++ b/lib/tty/key.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 int mou_auto_repeat = 100;      /* ms */
 int double_click_speed = 250;   /* ms */
-gboolean old_esc_mode = TRUE;
+gboolean old_esc_mode = FALSE;
 /* timeout for old_esc_mode in usec */
 int old_esc_mode_timeout = G_USEC_PER_SEC;      /* us, settable via env */
 gboolean use_8th_bit_as_meta = FALSE;
 
